// Phase 6b annotated all 292 top-level underscore functions in src/lib. This is
// the test that keeps that from being a no-op.
//
// The full suite's failure name set was IDENTICAL before and after the sweep,
// which is the right outcome — but it is also exactly what an unapplied
// annotation would produce, so on its own it proves nothing. This file is the
// other half: reaching a now-private stdlib helper from outside its module must
// be an error.
//
// `_lookup` is a plain Saffron function; test/fail/stdlib_private_extern.sf
// covers an @extern one, since those took a different route through the parser
// and were the 142 that Phase 6a had to unblock first.
import "@base64" as Base64

IO.println(Base64._lookup("abc", "a"))
